{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>I, before, etc., to speak to my heart.</b> He plundered [the word] טֶרֶם, for no ear heard — to impress upon the maiden that she should act in accordance with what she heard."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Hebrew שָׁלַל (he plundered) and לָחוּשׁ (to impress/whisper) are taken hyper-literally; the construction is elliptical, possibly meaning Eliezer 'seized upon' the fact that his prayer was silent (no ear heard it) to sensitively signal to Rebecca that she should act on what she perceived."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:11.293897774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}